/* ---- Privacy policy, readable offline ---- */
"about_privacy_policy" = "Privacy policy";
/* %1$@ = app version. Diverges (design.md §6): names the platform. */
"privacy_intro" = "Privacy policy for Arivu on iPhone, version %1$@.";
"privacy_short_title" = "The short version";
/* Diverges: the first paragraph carries the iOS form of the C3 claim (D-038). */
"privacy_short_body" = "Arivu has no code that can reach the internet. It contains no networking, and you can check that yourself, because Arivu is open source.\n\nWhat you type and what Arivu writes is stored only on your phone, in the app’s private storage. It is not included in iCloud backups or in a transfer to a new phone.\n\nWe do not collect, receive, sell or share your messages. There is no account, no advertising, no analytics and no crash-reporting software in the app.\n\nIf you choose to report a reply, Arivu writes an email with that reply and your note. You check it, and your own Mail app sends it. We receive only what you send.";
/* Diverges (design.md §6). */
"privacy_internet_title" = "Arivu has no way to reach the internet";
/* Diverges (design.md §6): the Android text enumerates permissions iOS does not have.
   Final text with Compliance (D-038). */
"privacy_internet_body" = "Arivu contains no networking code and links no networking library. There is nothing in it that opens a connection, and nothing that would work if it tried. Because Arivu is open source, anyone can read the code and rebuild it to check that the app on the App Store is the app in the source. The App Store privacy label says Data Not Collected, and that is the same claim in Apple’s words.";
"privacy_stored_title" = "What is stored on your phone";
/* Diverges (design.md §6): iPhone’s own encryption, iCloud backup and device transfer. */
"privacy_stored_body" = "Your conversation: the messages you send, the replies, when each was created, why a reply stopped, and whether you reported it. It is one file in Arivu’s private storage, kept until you delete Arivu. If that file is ever damaged, Arivu keeps only the newest damaged copy there and starts a new conversation.\n\nA note that your phone passed Arivu’s compatibility check, so the check does not run on every launch.\n\nThe file is excluded from iCloud backup and from transfers to a new phone. It is protected by your iPhone’s own encryption and your passcode. Anyone who can unlock your phone and open Arivu can read the conversation.";
"privacy_collect_title" = "What we collect";
"privacy_collect_body" = "Nothing, through the app. Arivu contains no analytics, advertising, tracking, crash-reporting or payment software, and it cannot send data. We never see your messages, and they are not used to train any AI model.";
"privacy_report_title" = "Reporting a reply";
/* Diverges (design.md §6): the composer opens inside Arivu; the fallback is the share sheet. */
"privacy_report_body" = "Under each reply there is a Report button, and there is a general Report button on this screen. Report opens a message in your own Mail app, inside Arivu, with our address, a subject and the app version already written. A report from under a reply also adds the reason you chose, your note and the text of that reply — only that reply, not the rest of the conversation. The general report on this screen is a blank form. Nothing is sent until you press send, and your Mail app, not Arivu, sends it. Arivu marks the reply as reported on your phone. If you have no mail account set up, Arivu offers the share sheet instead, with our address written into the text.\n\nIf you send a report, we receive what is in it and whatever your mail service adds, such as your email address. We use reports only to understand harmful replies, make Arivu safer and reply to you if needed. We do not sell or share them, and we delete them when we no longer need them. You can ask us to delete your report sooner.";
"privacy_copy_title" = "Copying text and your keyboard";
/* Diverges (design.md §6): Android can ask the keyboard not to learn; iOS offers no such request,
   and the text says so rather than implying we made one. */
"privacy_copy_body" = "Copy puts text on your phone’s clipboard, like any copied text. Your keyboard learns from what you type in every app, and iPhone gives Arivu no way to turn that off. Other apps work under their own privacy policies.";
/* Diverges (design.md §6): the App Store, not Google Play. */
"privacy_play_title" = "The App Store";
"privacy_play_body" = "You install and update Arivu through the App Store, which has its own privacy policy. Apple gives developers summary statistics, such as installs by country and device model, and crash statistics from people who chose to share them with Apple. Installing uses data. Once installed, Arivu itself uses none.";
"privacy_children_title" = "Children";
"privacy_children_body" = "Arivu is not designed for children. The app collects nothing from anyone. If a child has sent us a report, write to us and we will delete it.";
"privacy_choices_title" = "Your choices";
/* Diverges (design.md §6): there is no "clear storage" for one app on iOS. */
"privacy_choices_body" = "To delete your conversation, delete Arivu: touch and hold its icon on the Home Screen, then choose Delete App. iPhone has no way to clear one app’s storage without deleting the app. Arivu is open source, so anyone can check these claims. Depending on where you live, you may have further rights over a report you sent us, and you can complain to your data protection authority.";
"privacy_changes_title" = "Changes";
"privacy_changes_body" = "If a future version changes what Arivu stores or sends, this policy changes before that version is released. A version that needed the internet would be a different app, and we would say so plainly.";
